<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ RHOMBIC DRIVE SECTION ══ -->
<div class="p13-sep"></div>
<div class="p13-label">★ New — Rhombic Drive Generators</div>
<h2 class="p13-title">What rhombic drives add — and why they're ideal for steam pistons</h2>
<p class="p13-lead">
  A rhombic drive (Scotch-yoke rhombic linkage) converts piston reciprocating motion into perfectly smooth rotary motion with 
  zero side-thrust on the piston walls. Standard crank-drives produce lateral forces that wear piston rings. 
  Rhombic drives eliminate this: two counter-rotating cranks connected through a rhombus linkage cancel all lateral loads, 
  leaving only pure vertical piston force. For our two rear steam pistons, each gets its own rhombic drive unit 
  coupled to a dedicated generator. This adds ~+1,800W of additional electrical generation directly from 
  piston reciprocation — over and above what the six wheel/rail generators already produce.
</p>

<div class="g3">
  <div class="card green">
    <div class="badge volt">Physics of Rhombic Drive</div>
    <h3>Why Zero Side-Thrust Matters</h3>
    <p>In a conventional crank, the connecting rod angle creates a lateral force on the piston: F_side = F_piston × tan(θ). At 150 PSI this can reach 3–6 kN sideways — the main cause of piston ring wear and cylinder bore scoring.</p>
    <p>The rhombic linkage uses a diamond-shaped (rhombus) four-bar mechanism. At every crank angle, the lateral components cancel exactly. Net side force: zero. Piston lives 3–5× longer. Cylinder bore remains circular indefinitely.</p>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Piston side force (crank)</span><span>3,000–6,000 N</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Piston side force (rhombic)</span><span>0 N (exact)</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Cylinder bore wear rate reduction</span><span>~70–80%</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Piston ring life extension</span><span>3–5×</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card orange">
    <div class="badge orange">Rhombic Drive Generator Specs</div>
    <h3>Each Unit — Piston A + Piston B</h3>
    <p>Each rhombic drive unit couples its output shaft to a dedicated 150A / 48V generator. The counter-rotating cranks (180° phase offset from each other) provide near-constant torque delivery — the generator sees smooth input equivalent to a multi-cylinder engine.</p>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Drive type</span><span>Dual-crank rhombic linkage</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Piston stroke</span><span>120mm</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Crank throw</span><span>60mm</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Generator per unit</span><span>150A · 48V DC</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Raw output per unit</span><span>7,200W</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Real output (50% eff)</span><span>~1,800W each</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Combined both units</span><span>~3,600W additional</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Material (crank)</span><span>4340 chromoly steel</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Bearing type</span><span>Timken tapered roller</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Lubrication</span><span>Shared oil-bath circuit</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card gold">
    <div class="badge gold">Updated System Power Budget</div>
    <h3>Phase 13 Idle Surplus (With Rhombic Drives)</h3>
    <p>Adding two rhombic drive generators at 1,800W each to the Phase 12 idle surplus of +4,880W gives a total idle surplus of +8,480W. At cruise, the additional rhombic output (higher piston speed) adds ~2,800W more.</p>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Phase 12 idle surplus</span><span>+4,880W</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Rhombic drive A (idle)</span><span>+1,800W</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Rhombic drive B (idle)</span><span>+1,800W</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row teal"><span>Phase 13 idle SURPLUS</span><span>+8,480W ★★</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Phase 13 cruise surplus</span><span>~+12,000W</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Battery recharge (idle)</span><span>~4.7 hrs full charge</span></div>
  </div>
</div>

