<div class="p13-sep"></div>
<div class="p13-label">Phase 13 · New Component — Four-Wheel Air Disc Brake System</div>
<h2 class="p13-title">Compressed air repurposed from idle bootstrap → four-wheel pneumatic disc brakes</h2>
<p class="p13-lead">
  The compressed air tank (150 PSI) was used in Phase 11–12 as a cold-start piston bridge for 45–90 seconds. 
  In Phase 13, the dynamo concepts and CVT medium-idle solve cold-start without compressed air. 
  The compressor and tank are now fully dedicated to braking: a pneumatic four-disc system with ABS modulation, 
  proportioning valve, and regen braking path back to Battery A.
</p>

<div class="g3">
  <div class="card crimson">
    <div class="badge crimson">Air Compressor</div>
    <h3>Oil-Free Piston Compressor</h3>
    <p>A small belt-driven or electric oil-free compressor maintains reservoir pressure between 120–150 PSI. It activates automatically when reservoir drops below 120 PSI and shuts off at 150 PSI. This runs on Battery A — consumes ~350W when active (~5% duty cycle at cruise).</p>
    <div class="stat-row red"><span>Reservoir capacity</span><span>4-gallon tank</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Working pressure range</span><span>120–150 PSI</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Compressor draw</span><span>~350W when active</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Compressor duty cycle</span><span>~5% at cruise</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Full reservoir stops (est.)</span><span>~30–40 panic stops</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Recharge time after panic stop</span><span>~15 seconds</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card crimson">
    <div class="badge red">Brake Caliper Specs</div>
    <h3>4× Pneumatic Floating Disc Calipers</h3>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Front disc diameter</span><span>280mm</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Rear disc diameter</span><span>260mm</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Rotor material</span><span>Grey iron + SiC coating</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Pad material (primary)</span><span>Semi-metallic sintered</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Pad material (backup)</span><span>Ceramic compound</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Max rotor temp (continuous)</span><span>450°C (grey iron)</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Max rotor temp (panic stop)</span><span>650°C (peak, brief)</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Caliper piston bore</span><span>48mm (front) 42mm (rear)</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>ABS modulation</span><span>4-channel · PCW firmware</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Proportioning valve</span><span>Rear bias 65/35 F/R</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card blue">
    <div class="badge blue">Regen Braking Path</div>
    <h3>Brake Energy Recovery</h3>
    <p>When the operator lifts the throttle, the CVT transitions to engine-braking mode. The static engine's internal rotors slow against the steam pressure — this back-torque spins the generators in overspeed, pushing regenerative current back to Battery A. The pneumatic discs are the mechanical fallback and panic-stop system, not the primary energy-dissipation path.</p>
    <div class="stat-row blue"><span>Regen at moderate decel</span><span>~800–2,000W recovered</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Regen at 30 mph → 0</span><span>~1.2 kJ recovered</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>Air brake activation threshold</span><span>&gt;0.3g deceleration</span></div>
    <div class="stat-row"><span>ABS pressure pulse rate</span><span>8–12 Hz (wheel speed sensor)</span></div>
  </div>
</div>

