<div class="p13-sep"></div>
<div class="p13-label">Phase 13 · Bench Test Schedule — 12 Tests</div>
<h2 class="p13-title">No component advances to prototype without a passing bench result</h2>
<div class="test-grid">
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T1">
    <div class="badge volt">Priority ①</div>
    <h3>T-1 · Eddy Coil Exhaust Sleeve Bench Test</h3>
    <p>Validate actual output from opposing magnetic coils on a measured steam exhaust pipe replica.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Build 300mm sleeve with 12 coil pairs on ceramic former</li>
      <li>Route steam at 90 PSI, 120°C through sleeve at measured flow rate</li>
      <li>Measure output: expect 200–400W at idle conditions</li>
      <li>Measure at 150 PSI / high-velocity: expect 500–700W</li>
      <li>Measure back-pressure penalty: must be &lt;2%</li>
      <li>Thermal soak at 200°C for 4 hours: check coil insulation integrity</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: ≥200W at idle steam conditions with &lt;5% degradation after soak</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T2">
    <div class="badge orange">Priority ②</div>
    <h3>T-2 · Rhombic Drive Geometry Validation</h3>
    <p>Confirm zero side-thrust and smooth torque delivery before connecting to generator.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Machine prototype rhombic linkage from 4340 chromoly</li>
      <li>Mount on test piston at 150 PSI steam input</li>
      <li>Measure lateral piston force with strain gauges: must be &lt;50N</li>
      <li>Record torque ripple on output shaft: must be &lt;5% peak-to-peak</li>
      <li>Run 500 continuous cycles: check for link wear and clearance growth</li>
      <li>Measure bearing temperature under load: must stay &lt;80°C</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: &lt;50N side force, &lt;5% torque ripple, &lt;80°C bearings</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T3">
    <div class="badge gold">Priority ③</div>
    <h3>T-3 · CVT Prototype Adaptation</h3>
    <p>Adapt a commercial automotive CVT (e.g., Subaru TR690 or Nissan RE0F10A) to accept static engine shaft input.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Fabricate input adapter flange: static engine shaft → CVT primary pulley</li>
      <li>Bench-run at constant 500 RPM input; sweep output 0→1,200 RPM</li>
      <li>Measure CVT efficiency at each ratio: target ≥88% at cruise ratio</li>
      <li>Torque converter lock-up test: confirm slip below 50 RPM output</li>
      <li>Oil temperature test: shared circuit with engine — 4-hour run at max ratio</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: ≥88% efficiency, TC slips correctly, oil &lt;120°C after 4 hrs</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T4">
    <div class="badge volt">Priority ④</div>
    <h3>T-4 · Vacuum-Jacketed Boiler Pressure Test</h3>
    <p>Validate the ASME-rated inner vessel and vacuum jacket insulation before any steam operation.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Hydrostatic test inner vessel to 225 PSI (1.5× working pressure)</li>
      <li>Verify vacuum jacket achieves &lt;10 mTorr: thermal loss &lt;40% of non-jacketed</li>
      <li>Measure heat-up time from cold at 2,800W heater: target &lt;50 minutes</li>
      <li>Log pressure decay over 2-hour hold at 90 PSI with heater off</li>
      <li>Thermal cycling test: 10 cycles 20°C→230°C; check weld integrity</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: holds 225 PSI static, vacuum &lt;10 mTorr, ≤5 PSI decay/hour</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T5">
    <div class="badge orange">Priority ⑤</div>
    <h3>T-5 · Air Disc Brake System Bench Test</h3>
    <p>Validate pneumatic caliper actuation, ABS modulation, and fade resistance before vehicle installation.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Mount all 4 calipers on inertia dyno simulating 1,800 lb vehicle</li>
      <li>20 consecutive 60→0 mph stops: measure fade (peak deceleration must not drop &gt;15%)</li>
      <li>ABS trigger test: lock all 4 wheels, verify modulation at 8–12 Hz</li>
      <li>Thermal soak: rotor temperature after 10 consecutive stops; must be &lt;500°C</li>
      <li>Reservoir draw test: 30 consecutive stops; pressure must stay &gt;80 PSI throughout</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: &lt;15% fade, ABS modulates correctly, rotors &lt;500°C, pressure &gt;80 PSI</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T6">
    <div class="badge gold">Priority ⑥</div>
    <h3>T-6 · TEG Boiler Wrap Zone Layout Test</h3>
    <p>Measure actual TEG output from boiler exterior surface with zoned Peltier array.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Apply Zone A (inner, 180–230°C face) and Zone B (outer, 60–100°C face) arrays</li>
      <li>Measure output at steady-state boiler operation: target 800–1,400W combined</li>
      <li>Check TEG module adhesion after 50 thermal cycles: no delamination</li>
      <li>Measure efficiency degradation at maximum temperature: Bi₂Te₃ degrades above 250°C</li>
      <li>Confirm cold-side heat rejection to ambient without extra cooling</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: ≥700W at steady state, no delamination after 50 cycles</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T7">
    <div class="badge volt">Priority ⑦</div>
    <h3>T-7 · PCW Firmware Validation (PSI Floor + CVT Servo)</h3>
    <p>Validate that PCW enforces 90 PSI minimum and CVT servo loop tracks demand without hunting.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Simulate throttle command sweep: confirm PSI never commanded below 90 PSI</li>
      <li>CVT ratio servo response test: step demand change; settle within 200ms</li>
      <li>Overspeed protection test: simulate generator overspeed at 4,500 RPM; confirm shutdown</li>
      <li>Loss of sensor test: simulate pressure transducer failure; confirm failsafe (hold last good PSI)</li>
      <li>Watchdog timer test: force CPU halt; confirm hardware failsafe de-energizes relief valve</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: PSI floor never breached, CVT settles &lt;200ms, all failsafes trigger correctly</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T8">
    <div class="badge orange">Priority ⑧</div>
    <h3>T-8 · Rhombic Drive Generator Output Verification</h3>
    <p>Confirm actual electrical output from each rhombic drive generator under steam piston conditions.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Connect Gen-Rhomb-A and Gen-Rhomb-B to calibrated load bank</li>
      <li>Steam at 90 PSI (idle): measure combined output; target ≥2,400W</li>
      <li>Steam at 150 PSI (full throttle): target ≥3,000W combined</li>
      <li>Measure generator temperature after 30-minute sustained run: &lt;90°C winding</li>
      <li>Verify DC bus stability: voltage ripple &lt;2% after rectification</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: ≥2,400W at idle PSI, &lt;90°C windings, &lt;2% ripple</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T9">
    <div class="badge gold">Priority ⑨</div>
    <h3>T-9 · Stirling Auxiliary Engine Output</h3>
    <p>Measure actual Stirling output from boiler flank thermal differential.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Bolt Stirling to boiler exterior at steady 180°C wall temperature</li>
      <li>Measure electrical output at ambient 25°C cold side: target 400–600W</li>
      <li>Check Stirling operation at minimum boiler temp (90 PSI ≈ 175°C): must still produce &gt;300W</li>
      <li>Run 24-hour continuous: monitor power output stability (±10% acceptable)</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: ≥400W at operating temp, ≥300W at minimum temp, &lt;10% drift over 24hrs</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T10">
    <div class="badge volt">Priority ⑩</div>
    <h3>T-10 · Closed-Loop Self-Sustain Endurance Test</h3>
    <p>The critical test: run the full system for 4 hours in closed-loop and verify battery SOC holds or rises.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Start with battery at 50% SOC</li>
      <li>Run at medium idle (90 PSI) for 2 hours: log SOC at every 10 minutes</li>
      <li>Run at cruise equivalent (120 PSI) for 2 hours: log all power nodes</li>
      <li>Measure water consumption and condensate recovery rate</li>
      <li>Log all component temperatures at 1-minute intervals</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: SOC rises during idle; SOC rises faster at cruise; water recovery ≥80%</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T11">
    <div class="badge orange">Priority ⑪</div>
    <h3>T-11 · PTFE Hose Pressure + Temperature Life Test</h3>
    <p>Validate that PTFE braided stainless flex lines survive 20,000 miles equivalent thermal cycling.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Pressure cycle test: 0→150 PSI, 200,000 cycles (equiv. ~20K miles piston strokes)</li>
      <li>Temperature cycle test: 25°C→230°C, 5,000 cycles</li>
      <li>Burst pressure test after cycling: must exceed 400 PSI (2.67× working pressure)</li>
      <li>Inspect braid for fretting at fittings after all cycles</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: &gt;400 PSI burst, no braid fretting, no inner liner cracks</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="test-card" data-num="T12">
    <div class="badge gold">Priority ⑫</div>
    <h3>T-12 · MHD Sleeve Lab Validation (Experimental)</h3>
    <p>Validate K₂CO₃ ionization seeding mechanism at required steam temperatures before vehicle consideration.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Lab bench: seed steam with 0.1–0.5% K₂CO₃ by mass</li>
      <li>Measure ionization fraction at 200°C, 230°C: expect &lt;0.1% ionization</li>
      <li>Apply 0.5 T magnetic field; measure induced current in external coil</li>
      <li>Scale projection: if &gt;50W measured at bench, proceed to sleeve design</li>
      <li>If &lt;50W, classify MHD as Phase 14+ only (insufficient at steam temperatures)</li>
      <li>Pass/fail: &gt;50W bench output with 0.5T field and 0.5% K₂CO₃ seeding</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

